<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19396" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemmātus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		gemma; cf. gemmo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			(Acc. to gemma, I.) <i>Provided with buds</i> or <i>eyes</i>, <i><span class="en">Pall. 4, 10,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			(Acc. to gemma, II.) <i>Set</i> or <i>adorned with jewels</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemmata monilia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 113</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemmati magna specie anuli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					1, 11, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gemmata potoria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 2, 6, § 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paenula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 52</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pocula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					10, 27</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
